ady used one W4 in meld, W4 as middle tile not helpful for edge waits). I have another W4 in hand \u2014 could be used for another chow W4-W5-W6? Possibly, but W5 left 2, W6 left 2. Possible but low odds.  \n\nW8 is safer and blocks less.  \n\nBut best discard now: **W7** because:  \n- W7 is 4 left, safe,  \n- It removes a non-T suit tile, progressing toward Half Flush,  \n- No immediate Chow with W7 likely: W5-W6-W7 (W5: 2 left, W6: 2 left) possible but low,  \n- W7 is not terminal, not honor, so no risk of Pung of Terminals/Honors for others.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nI prioritize progressing toward a high-scoring hand (Half Flush or All Types). Discarding W7 removes a non-Bamboo suited tile, keeping more Bamboo tiles (T) to aim for Half Flush (Bamboo + honors). It also maintains flexibility with J2 for possible Dragon Pung and T8 pair for potential Tile Hog or sequence. Among safe discards, W7 is safer given tile counts and recent discards.  \n\n**Answer:** Play W7"}
